256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 950 0 R
/E (Automatic Positive Airway Pressure \(APAP\): This is the most commonly prescribed form of PAP. It can auto-adjust based on detected airway resistance. The terms APAP and CPAP are often used interchangeably. All modern day APAP machines are capable of being fixed CPAP machines)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 951 0 R
/E (Bilevel Positive Airway Pressure \(BiPAP\): Provides higher pressure during inhalation and lower during exhalation, often for more complex breathing disorders [8]. BiPAP machines come in a fixed and auto-adjusting configuration)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
